srow(43, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND I WILL GIVE GRASS IN YOUR FIELD FOR YOUR CATTLE" (11:15) — THAT YOU BE NOT TROUBLED TO THE DESERTS. YOU SAY SO, OR IS IT LITERAL? "AND YOU SHALL EAT AND BE SATISFIED" — SO WHAT DO I MAKE OF THE GRASS? THAT YOU BE NOT TROUBLED TO THE DESERTS. The head row of piska 43 ({SP_(43, 1, "שלא", "תהא", "מצטער", "למדברות")} "that you be not troubled to the deserts"): I12 (the context decides — the eating clause fixes the grass clause; checked). Fresh in both files.')
srow(43, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'R. JUDAH BEN BAVA: "GRASS IN YOUR FIELD FOR YOUR CATTLE" — BETWEEN THE BOUNDARIES. R. SHIMON BEN YOHAI: THAT YOU CUT AND THROW BEFORE YOUR CATTLE ALL THE RAINY DAYS, AND WITHHOLD YOUR HAND THIRTY DAYS BEFORE THE HARVEST — AND IT YIELDS, NOT LESS THAN ITS GRAIN. The two readings ({SP_(43, 2, "בין", "התחומים")} "between the boundaries"; {SP_(43, 2, "קודם", "לקציר", "שלשים", "יום")} "thirty days before the harvest"): the thirty days a datum (the grazing of the standing grain). Fresh.')
srow(43, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'RABBI: "GRASS IN YOUR FIELD FOR YOUR CATTLE" — THIS IS FLAX; "WHO MAKES GRASS GROW FOR THE CATTLE AND HERB FOR MAN\'S LABOR" (PSALM 104:14). ({SP_(43, 3, "זה", "פשתן")} "this is flax"). Fresh.')
srow(43, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND YOU SHALL EAT AND BE SATISFIED" — A GOOD SIGN FOR A MAN WHEN HIS BEAST EATS AND IS SATISFIED; "THE RIGHTEOUS KNOWS THE SOUL OF HIS BEAST" (PROVERBS 12:10). ({SP_(43, 4, "סימן", "טוב", "לאדם")} "a good sign for a man"). Fresh.')
srow(43, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'ANOTHER WORD: WHEN YOUR BEAST EATS AND IS SATISFIED IT WORKS THE GROUND WITH STRENGTH — "MUCH INCREASE BY THE STRENGTH OF THE OX" (PROVERBS 14:4). ({SP_(43, 5, "עובדת", "בכח", "האדמה")} "it works the ground with strength"). Fresh.')
srow(43, 6, 'CONTEXT', f'ANOTHER WORD: "AND YOU SHALL EAT AND BE SATISFIED" — FROM THE OFFSPRING; NO PROOF, BUT A HINT — "THEY SHALL FLOW TO THE GOODNESS OF THE LORD, TO THE GRAIN, THE WINE AND THE OIL" (JEREMIAH 31:11-12). ({SP_(43, 6, "מן", "הולדות")} "from the offspring"). Fresh.')
srow(43, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL EAT AND BE SATISFIED — TAKE HEED TO YOURSELVES LEST YOUR HEART BE DECEIVED" (11:15-16): HE SAID TO THEM, BE WARNED LEST YOU REBEL AGAINST THE ALL-PRESENT, FOR A MAN REBELS ONLY OUT OF SATIETY — "LEST YOU EAT AND BE SATISFIED AND BUILD GOOD HOUSES … AND YOUR SILVER AND GOLD MULTIPLY" (8:12-13) AND THEN? "YOUR HEART BE LIFTED UP AND YOU FORGET" (8:14); "WHEN I BRING HIM TO THE LAND FLOWING WITH MILK AND HONEY" (31:20) AND THEN? "HE WILL TURN TO OTHER GODS"; "THE PEOPLE SAT TO EAT AND DRINK" (EXODUS 32:6) AND THEN? "THEY MADE A MOLTEN CALF" (32:8). THE SATIETY THAT REBELS ({SP_(43, 7, "הזהרו", "שמא", "תמרדו", "במקום")} "be warned lest you rebel against the All-Present"; {SP_(43, 7, "אלא", "מתוך", "שובע")} "only out of satiety"): E28 (the verse read from the one before it — checked): 11:16\'s caution read as 11:15\'s consequence; chapter 8\'s row (read there on 8:12-14, reread whole here), the calf\'s Exodus 32:6-8 the third proof. REREAD WHOLE.')
srow(43, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'SO THE FLOOD\'S GENERATION REBELLED ONLY OUT OF SATIETY — "THEIR HOUSES ARE SAFE FROM FEAR … THEY SPEND THEIR DAYS IN PROSPERITY" (JOB 21:9-13), AND IT CAUSED THEM: "THEY SAID TO GOD, DEPART FROM US" (21:14-15) — WE NEED NOT A DROP OF RAIN, "A MIST RISES FROM THE EARTH" (GENESIS 2:6); THE ALL-PRESENT: BY THE GOOD I DID YOU, YOU EXALT YOURSELVES — BY IT I WILL PUNISH YOU: "THE RAIN WAS ON THE EARTH FORTY DAYS AND FORTY NIGHTS" (7:12). R. YOSE BEN DORMASKIT: THEY SET THEIR EYES ABOVE AND BELOW TO DO THEIR LUST, SO HE OPENED ON THEM THE UPPER AND LOWER SPRINGS — "ALL THE FOUNTAINS OF THE GREAT DEEP WERE BROKEN AND THE WINDOWS OF HEAVEN OPENED" (7:11). The flood from satiety ({SP_(43, 8, "טפה", "אחת", "של", "גשמים", "היא")} "it is one drop of rain"; {SP_(43, 8, "הם", "נתנו", "עיניהם", "עליונה", "ותחתונה")} "they set their eyes above and below"): THE RAIN AS THE INSTRUMENT OF THE REBELLION AND THE PUNISHMENT — the flood\'s גשם ("rain") the ink measured (Genesis 7:12 the noun\'s Torah seat); the measure-for-measure named, no code. Read before at two Genesis sittings (gen_08, gen_17 — the boarding), REREAD WHOLE here.')
srow(43, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'SO THE MEN OF THE TOWER REBELLED ONLY OUT OF SATIETY — "THE WHOLE EARTH WAS OF ONE LANGUAGE … THEY FOUND A PLAIN IN SHINAR AND SETTLED THERE" (GENESIS 11:1-2): THE SETTLING SAID HERE IS EATING AND DRINKING, AS "THE PEOPLE SAT TO EAT AND DRINK AND ROSE TO PLAY" (EXODUS 32:6); IT CAUSED THEM: "COME, LET US BUILD A CITY" (11:4) — "AND THE LORD SCATTERED THEM" (11:8). The tower from satiety ({SP_(43, 9, "ואין", "ישיבה", "האמורה", "כאן", "אלא", "אכילה", "ושתיה")} "and the settling said here is only eating and drinking"): I2 (the verbal analogy on "sat/settled" from the calf — checked); the Sifrei on Numbers 131 in the note. Read before at the Babel sitting (gen_25), REREAD WHOLE here.')
srow(43, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'SO THE MEN OF SODOM REBELLED ONLY OUT OF SATIETY — "A LAND FROM WHICH COMES BREAD … ITS STONES SAPPHIRE" (JOB 28:5-8): THEY SAID, WE HAVE FOOD, SILVER AND GOLD — LET US BLOT OUT THE LAW OF THE WAYFARER FROM OUR LAND; THE ALL-PRESENT: BY THE GOOD I DID YOU, YOU WOULD FORGET THE WAYFARER\'S LAW — I WILL MAKE YOU FORGOTTEN FROM THE WORLD: "A STREAM BREAKS OUT FAR FROM THE SOJOURNER" (28:4), "THE TENTS OF ROBBERS PROSPER" (JOB 12:5-6); "THIS WAS THE INIQUITY OF SODOM YOUR SISTER … SHE DID NOT STRENGTHEN THE HAND OF THE POOR" (EZEKIEL 16:48-49). Sodom from satiety ({SP_(43, 10, "הרי", "מזון", "אצלינו")} "we have food"; {SP_(43, 10, "ונשכח", "תורת", "הרגל", "מארצנו")} "and forget the law of the wayfarer from our land"): the Tosefta Sotah 3 in the note; no code. Fresh.')
srow(43, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'LIKEWISE "FOR IT WAS ALL WATERED" (GENESIS 13:10) — AND THEN? "THEY MADE THEIR FATHER DRINK WINE" (19:33): WHENCE WINE IN THE CAVE? IT WAS PROVIDED FOR THE HOUR, "THE MOUNTAINS SHALL DRIP SWEET WINE" (JOEL 4:18) — IF SO TO THOSE WHO ANGER HIM, HOW MUCH MORE TO THOSE WHO DO HIS WILL. R. MEIR: "WHITE, GREEN AND BLUE HANGINGS" (ESTHER 1:6) — WHY TEACH AHASUERUS\' WEALTH? IF SO TO THOSE WHO ANGER HIM, HOW MUCH MORE TO THOSE WHO DO HIS WILL. Lot\'s plain and the wine ({SP_(43, 11, "ומאין", "היה", "להן", "יין", "במערה")} "and whence had they wine in the cave"; {SP_(43, 11, "אם", "כך", "נתן", "למכעיסיו")} "if so He gave to those who anger Him"): I1 (checked) twice; the paronomasia on "watered" / "made drink" named; R. Meir\'s Esther the English marks as a possible interpolation from Esther Rabbah (F:94 n.7) — read and marked, kept in the row. Read before at gen_29 (Lot\'s plain), REREAD WHOLE here.')
srow(43, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'RABBAN GAMLIEL, R. JOSHUA, R. ELAZAR BEN AZARIAH AND R. AKIVA ENTERING ROME HEARD THE CITY\'S ROAR FROM PUTEOLI, A HUNDRED AND TWENTY MIL — THEY WEPT AND R. AKIVA LAUGHED: THE NATIONS WHO SERVE IDOLS DWELL SECURE, AND THE FOOTSTOOL OF OUR GOD IS BURNT AND A DEN OF BEASTS — "THAT IS WHY I LAUGH: IF SO TO THOSE WHO ANGER HIM, HOW MUCH MORE TO THOSE WHO DO HIS WILL". Akiva at Rome ({SP_(43, 12, "נכנסים", "לרומי")} "entering Rome"; {SP_(43, 12, "התחילו", "הם", "בוכים", "ורבי", "עקיבה", "מצחק")} "they began weeping and R. Akiva laughing"): I1 (checked); no citation in either file (asserted); Makkot 24b\'s seat (the docket\'s); the hundred and twenty mil a datum. Fresh.')
srow(43, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'AGAIN, GOING UP TO JERUSALEM — AT SCOPUS THEY TORE THEIR GARMENTS; AT THE TEMPLE MOUNT A FOX CAME OUT OF THE HOLY OF HOLIES — THEY WEPT AND R. AKIVA LAUGHED: "THE STRANGER WHO COMES NEAR SHALL DIE" (NUMBERS 1:51) — AND A FOX COMES OUT OF IT; "FOR MOUNT ZION DESOLATE, FOXES WALK ON IT" (LAMENTATIONS 5:17-18). AKIVA: "I WILL TAKE ME FAITHFUL WITNESSES, URIAH THE PRIEST AND ZECHARIAH" (ISAIAH 8:2) — URIAH: "ZION SHALL BE PLOWED AS A FIELD" (JEREMIAH 26:18); ZECHARIAH: "OLD MEN AND OLD WOMEN SHALL YET SIT IN THE STREETS OF JERUSALEM" (ZECHARIAH 8:4): IF URIAH\'S WORDS STAND, ZECHARIAH\'S STAND — I REJOICE THAT URIAH\'S WERE FULFILLED, FOR ZECHARIAH\'S ARE TO COME. "AKIVA, YOU HAVE CONSOLED US." The fox and the two witnesses ({SP_(43, 13, "וראו", "שועל", "יוצא", "מבית", "קדש", "הקדשים")} "and they saw a fox coming out of the Holy of Holies"; {SP_(43, 13, "עקיבה", "נחמתנו")} "Akiva, you have consoled us"): the two prophecies bound as one witness-pair (Isaiah 8:2 read of Jeremiah 26:18 and Zechariah 8:4 — the anachronism the shelf\'s own); Makkot 24b the docket\'s. Fresh.')
srow(43, 14, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "AND YOU SHALL EAT AND BE SATISFIED — TAKE HEED TO YOURSELVES": BE WARNED LEST THE EVIL INCLINATION LEAD YOU ASTRAY AND YOU SEPARATE FROM THE TORAH — FOR ONCE A MAN SEPARATES FROM THE TORAH HE GOES AND CLEAVES TO IDOLATRY: "THEY HAVE TURNED ASIDE QUICKLY FROM THE WAY … THEY HAVE MADE A MOLTEN CALF" (EXODUS 32:8); DAVID — "THEY HAVE DRIVEN ME OUT … SAYING, GO SERVE OTHER GODS" (1 SAMUEL 26:19): WOULD DAVID SERVE IDOLS? ONCE HE CEASES FROM WORDS OF TORAH HE GOES AND CLEAVES TO IDOLATRY. The road from Torah to the idols ({SP_(43, 14, "שמא", "יטעה", "אתכם", "יצר", "הרע")} "lest the evil inclination lead you astray"; {SP_(43, 14, "הולך", "ומדבק", "בעבודה", "זרה")} "goes and cleaves to idolatry"): the calf\'s formula (Exodus 32:8 — 11:28\'s "turn aside from the way", computed) the proof; the inclination\'s name chapter 10\'s (the docket\'s Sukkah 52a). Fresh.')
srow(43, 15, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND YOU TURN ASIDE" — FROM THE WAY OF LIFE TO THE WAY OF DEATH. ({SP_(43, 15, "מדרך", "חיים", "לדרך", "מות")} "from the way of life to the way of death"); 54:3 repeats it on 11:28. Fresh.')
srow(43, 16, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND SERVE OTHER GODS" — ARE THEY GODS? "THEY HAVE PUT THEIR GODS IN THE FIRE, FOR THEY WERE NO GODS" (ISAIAH 37:19). WHY "OTHER" (ACHERIM)? THEY DELAY (ME\'ACHARIM) THE GOOD FROM COMING INTO THE WORLD; ANOTHER WORD: THEY MAKE THEIR WORSHIPPERS OTHERS; ANOTHER: OTHERS CALL THEM GODS. The name "other" read three ways ({SP_(43, 16, "שמאחרים", "את", "הטובה")} "that they delay the good"; {SP_(43, 16, "שעושים", "את", "עובדיהם", "אחרים")} "that they make their worshippers others"): the sound-play named, no code; the Mekhilta parallels in the note. Fresh.')
srow(43, 17, 'CONTEXT', f'ANOTHER WORD: "OTHER GODS" — THEY ARE OTHERS TO THEIR WORSHIPPERS, "HE CRIES TO IT AND IT DOES NOT ANSWER, NOR SAVE HIM FROM HIS TROUBLE" (ISAIAH 46:7). ({SP_(43, 17, "שאחרים", "הם", "לעובדיהם")} "that they are others to their worshippers"). Fresh.')
srow(43, 18, 'MATERIAL', f'R. YOSE: WHY "OTHER GODS"? SO THAT NONE SAY, HAD THEY BEEN CALLED BY HIS NAME THERE WOULD BE USE IN THEM — THEY WERE CALLED BY HIS NAME AND THERE WAS NO USE: IN THE DAYS OF ENOSH SON OF SETH, "THEN WAS THE NAME OF THE LORD CALLED UPON" (GENESIS 4:26). Enosh\'s naming ({SP_(43, 18, "בימי", "אנוש", "בן", "שת")} "in the days of Enosh son of Seth"): the Genesis sitting\'s row (gen_13 — Cain\'s line and Seth), REREAD WHOLE here; 43:19 continues it.')
srow(43, 19, 'MATERIAL', f'AT THAT HOUR THE OCEAN ROSE AND FLOODED A THIRD OF THE WORLD — THE HOLY ONE SAID: YOU DID A NEW THING AND CALLED FOR YOURSELVES, I TOO WILL DO A NEW THING AND CALL FOR MYSELF — "WHO CALLS THE WATERS OF THE SEA AND POURS THEM OUT" (AMOS 5:8). R. ISAAC: WERE THE IDOLS\' NAMES SPELLED OUT, ALL THE HIDES OF THE WORLD WOULD NOT SUFFICE. R. ELIEZER: WHY "OTHER"? THEY MAKE THEMSELVES A NEW GOD EVERY DAY — GOLD NEEDED, SILVER; SILVER, BRONZE; BRONZE, IRON; IRON, TIN; TIN, LEAD; LEAD, WOOD. Enosh\'s flood and the daily god ({SP_(43, 19, "עלה", "אוקיינוס", "והציף", "שלישו", "של", "עולם")} "the Ocean rose and flooded a third of the world"; {SP_(43, 19, "שמחדשים", "להם", "אלוהות", "בכל", "יום")} "that they renew for themselves a god every day"): THE SHELF\'S VERB "FLOODED" (והציף) IS THE CHAPTER\'S OWN — 11:4\'s "made the waters flow" (הציף), the hiphil\'s one seat in the Bible (computed): the shelf uses the sea\'s verb of Enosh\'s ocean; the seven metals a DATA row. Read before at the creation sitting (gen_01), REREAD WHOLE here.')
srow(43, 20, 'CONTEXT', f'R. HANINA BEN ANTIGONOS: SEE THE WORD THE TORAH TOOK — "MOLECH": WHATEVER YOU MAKE KING (TAMLICHEHU) OVER YOU, EVEN FOR ONE HOUR. ({SP_(43, 20, "מולך", "כל", "שתמליכהו", "עליך")} "Molech — whatever you make king over you"); the name for its sound, no code; no citation in either file. Fresh.')
srow(43, 21, 'CONTEXT', f'RABBI: WHY "OTHER GODS"? THEY ARE LATER (ACHERIM) THAN THE LAST OF THE WORKS — HE WHO IS LAST IN THE WORKS CALLED THEM GODS. ({SP_(43, 21, "אחרים", "לאחרון", "שבמעשים")} "others to the last of the works"); no citation. Fresh.')
srow(43, 22, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND BOW DOWN TO THEM" — TO THEM YOU BOW, TO ME YOU DO NOT BOW: "THEY BOWED TO IT AND SACRIFICED TO IT AND SAID, THESE ARE YOUR GODS, O ISRAEL" (EXODUS 32:8). OTHERS SAY: HAD ISRAEL NOT JOINED THE NAME OF THE ALL-PRESENT TO THE IDOLATRY, THEY WOULD HAVE PERISHED FROM THE WORLD. RABBAN SHIMON BEN GAMLIEL: WHOEVER JOINS HIS NAME TO IDOLATRY IS BOUND TO PERISH — "HE WHO SACRIFICES TO THE GODS SHALL BE DESTROYED" (EXODUS 22:19)! WHAT DOES "OTHER GODS" TEACH? THAT THEY MADE MANY CALVES — "THEY SHUT THE DOORS OF THE PORCH … NEITHER INCENSE NOR BURNT OFFERING IN THE SANCTUARY TO THE GOD OF ISRAEL" (2 CHRONICLES 29:7): TO ANOTHER THING THEY OFFERED. The bowing ({SP_(43, 22, "להם", "אתם", "משתחוים", "לי", "אי", "אתם", "משתחוים")} "to them you bow, to Me you do not bow"; {SP_(43, 22, "שעשו", "להם", "עגלים", "הרבה")} "that they made themselves many calves"): the calf\'s Exodus 32:8 twice in the piska (the ink\'s calf formula); the "others" dispute the English marks difficult (Mekhilta Nezikin 17 the parallel); the plural "gods" read as many calves — the plural rule, no code. Fresh.')
srow(43, 23, 'MATERIAL', f'"IF YOU DO SO — AND THE ANGER OF THE LORD BE KINDLED AGAINST YOU" (11:17). THE PARABLE OF THE KING WHO SENT HIS SON TO A BANQUET AND CHARGED HIM NOT TO EAT OR DRINK MORE THAN HIS NEED; THE SON DID NOT HEED, VOMITED AND FOULED THE GUESTS, AND THEY THREW HIM BEHIND THE PALACE. SO THE HOLY ONE TO ISRAEL: I BROUGHT YOU INTO A GOOD AND BROAD LAND FLOWING WITH MILK AND HONEY TO EAT ITS FRUIT, BE SATISFIED WITH ITS GOOD AND BLESS MY NAME ON IT — YOU WERE NOT IN THE GOOD; BE IN THE RETRIBUTION. The banquet ({SP_(43, 23, "משל", "למלך", "ששגר", "את", "בנו", "לבית", "המשתה")} "a parable of a king who sent his son to the banquet"; {SP_(43, 23, "לא", "הייתם", "בטובה", "היו", "בפורענות")} "you were not in the good, be in the retribution"): E26 (checked); 11:17 cited by name (asserted); "to bless My Name on it" — 8:10\'s grace (chapter 8\'s compile) the shelf\'s own term. Fresh.')
srow(43, 24, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE ANGER OF THE LORD BE KINDLED AGAINST YOU" — SHALL THEY BE FINISHED FROM THE WORLD? "AND HE SHUT THE HEAVENS": THE KINDS OF RETRIBUTION ARE FINISHED, NOT THEY — "MY ARROWS I WILL FINISH ON THEM" (32:23): THE ARROWS FINISH, THEY DO NOT; "THE LORD HAS FINISHED HIS FURY" (LAMENTATIONS 4:11). The arrows finished ({SP_(43, 24, "מיני", "פרעניות", "הם", "כלים")} "the kinds of retribution are finished"; {SP_(43, 24, "חצי", "כלים", "והם", "אינם", "כלים")} "My arrows are finished and they are not finished"): the shut heavens read as a bounded retribution (the English notes the material poorly attested — read and marked). Fresh.')
srow(43, 25, 'MATERIAL', f'"HEAT OF ANGER" IS SAID HERE AND "HEAT OF ANGER" THERE (EXODUS 22:23) — AS THERE THE SWORD, SO HERE THE SWORD; AS THERE (LEVITICUS 26:16) PLAGUE AND WILD BEAST, SO HERE; AS HERE DROUGHT AND EXILE, SO THERE: WHEREVER "HEAT OF ANGER" IS SAID, FIVE KINDS OF RETRIBUTION — SWORD, PLAGUE, WILD BEAST, DROUGHT AND EXILE. THE FIVE RETRIBUTIONS ({SP_(43, 25, "נאמר", "כאן", "חרי", "אף")} "heat of anger is said here"; {SP_(43, 25, "חמשה", "מיני", "פרעניות", "הם")} "five kinds of retribution they are"): I2 (the verbal analogy on "heat of anger" across Exodus 22:23, Leviticus 26:16 and 11:17 — checked) running BOTH WAYS, the five the sum — a DATA row for the compile\'s effect (the anger\'s content; the Mekhilta Nezikin 18 the parallel); the fold\'s Leviticus 26 a third time. Fresh.')
srow(43, 26, 'CONTEXT', f'ANOTHER WORD: "AGAINST YOU" — AND NOT AGAINST THE NATIONS OF THE WORLD, WHO SIT IN THE GOOD WHILE ISRAEL SITS IN RETRIBUTION: THE NATIONS DO NOT BURY THEIR SONS AND DAUGHTERS, ISRAEL BURIES THEM. ({SP_(43, 26, "ולא", "באמות", "העולם")} "and not against the nations of the world"). Fresh.')
srow(43, 27, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE SHUT THE HEAVENS" — THE CLOUDS LADEN AND STANDING, LETTING DOWN NOT A DROP; WHENCE EVEN DEWS AND WINDS? "I WILL MAKE YOUR HEAVENS AS IRON" (LEVITICUS 26:19); OR THE IRRIGATED FIELD BEAR FRUIT? "AND YOUR LAND AS BRASS". The heavens shut ({SP_(43, 27, "שיהו", "עננים", "טעונים", "ועומדים")} "that the clouds be laden and standing"): the fold\'s Leviticus 26:19 the proof — the shut heavens and the iron heavens the same effect (the compile\'s heaven_shut by CALL). Fresh.')
srow(43, 28, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE GROUND NOT GIVE ITS PRODUCE" — NOT EVEN WHAT FALLS OF ITSELF; "ITS PRODUCE" — EVEN WHAT YOU BRING TO IT; OR THE TREE BEAR FRUIT? "THE TREE OF THE FIELD SHALL NOT GIVE ITS FRUIT" (LEVITICUS 26:20); OR WOOD FOR THE OVEN? "SHALL NOT GIVE ITS FRUIT"; OR GO ABROAD AND SIT IN THE GOOD? "YOUR HEAVENS OVER YOUR HEAD SHALL BE BRASS AND THE EARTH UNDER YOU IRON" (28:23) — EVERYWHERE. The produce withheld ({SP_(43, 28, "אף", "לא", "נפלה")} "not even what falls"; {SP_(43, 28, "בכל", "מקום")} "in every place"): the sound-play "its produce / what you bring it" named (the note: assonance alone); Leviticus 26:20 and 28:23 the proofs — the curse follows abroad. Fresh.')
srow(43, 29, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "AND THE ANGER OF THE LORD" — AFTER ALL THE AFFLICTIONS I BRING ON YOU, I EXILE YOU; EXILE IS HARD, WEIGHED AGAINST ALL: "THE LORD PLUCKED THEM FROM THEIR LAND IN ANGER AND CAST THEM INTO ANOTHER LAND" (29:27); "THOSE FOR DEATH TO DEATH, FOR THE SWORD TO THE SWORD, FOR FAMINE TO FAMINE, FOR CAPTIVITY TO CAPTIVITY" (JEREMIAH 15:2); "ISRAEL SHALL SURELY GO INTO EXILE" (AMOS 7:17); "WEEP NOT FOR THE DEAD … WEEP FOR HIM WHO GOES AWAY" (JEREMIAH 22:10) — "WEEP NOT FOR THE DEAD": JEHOIAKIM, "BURIED WITH THE BURIAL OF AN ASS" (22:19). Exile the last ({SP_(43, 29, "קשה", "גלות", "ששקולה", "כנגד", "הכל")} "exile is hard, weighed against all"): the retribution\'s order — the compile\'s DATA (the exile the fifth of 43:25\'s five). Fresh.')
srow(43, 30, 'CONTEXT', f'"WEEP FOR HIM WHO GOES AWAY" — JEHOIACHIN: "HE CHANGED HIS PRISON GARMENTS" (JEREMIAH 52:33): JEHOIAKIM\'S CARCASS, CAST TO THE HEAT BY DAY AND THE FROST BY NIGHT, WAS DEARER THAN THE LIFE OF JEHOIACHIN, WHOSE THRONE WAS ABOVE THE KINGS\' AND WHO ATE AT THE KINGS\' TABLE. ({SP_(43, 30, "זה", "יהויכין", "מלך", "יהודה")} "this is Jehoiachin king of Judah"). Fresh.')
srow(43, 31, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU PERISH QUICKLY" — AT ONCE I EXILE YOU AND GIVE YOU NO EXTENSION; IF YOU SAY, THE FLOOD\'S MEN WERE GIVEN A HUNDRED AND TWENTY YEARS — THEY HAD NONE TO LEARN FROM, YOU HAVE ONE TO LEARN FROM. Quickly, no extension ({SP_(43, 31, "מיד", "אני", "מגלה", "אתכם")} "at once I exile you"; {SP_(43, 31, "מאה", "ועשרים", "שנה")} "a hundred and twenty years"): Genesis 6:3\'s hundred and twenty the datum (the flood prologue\'s sitting — gen_15, read there and reread whole here); the English supplies "namely, Moses" for the teacher. REREAD WHOLE.')
srow(43, 32, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "AND YOU PERISH QUICKLY" — EXILE AFTER EXILE: SO THE TEN TRIBES, SO JUDAH AND BENJAMIN — EXILED IN NEBUCHADNEZZAR\'S SEVENTH YEAR, HIS EIGHTEENTH AND HIS TWENTY-THIRD. R. JOSHUA BEN KORHAH: THE ROBBER WHO ENTERED THE OWNER\'S FIELD AND CUT A BASKETFUL, AND THE OWNER DID NOT MIND; CUT THE STANDING GRAIN, AND HE DID NOT MIND; UNTIL HE HEAPED HIS BASKET AND LEFT — "THE FORMER LIGHTLY AFFLICTED THE LAND OF ZEBULUN AND NAPHTALI, THE LATTER DEALT HEAVILY" (ISAIAH 8:23). Exile after exile ({SP_(43, 32, "גולה", "אחר", "גולה")} "exile after exile"; {SP_(43, 32, "משל", "ללסטיס")} "a parable of a robber"): E26 (checked); THE THREE EXILES DATED — Nebuchadnezzar\'s 7th, 18th and 23rd years (Jeremiah 52:28-30\'s data) — a DATA row for the clock. Fresh.')
srow(43, 33, 'CONTEXT', f'R. SHIMON BEN YOHAI: IF THOSE OF WHOM "QUICKLY" WAS SAID WERE EXILED ONLY AFTER A TIME, HOW MUCH MORE THOSE OF WHOM "QUICKLY" WAS NOT SAID. ({SP_(43, 33, "קל", "וחומר", "למי", "שלא", "נאמר", "בהם", "מהרה")} "how much more those of whom quickly was not said"); I1 (checked). Fresh.')
srow(43, 34, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "AND YOU PERISH QUICKLY … AND YOU SHALL PUT THESE MY WORDS" (11:17-18) — THOUGH I EXILE YOU FROM THE LAND ABROAD, BE MARKED BY THE COMMANDMENTS, THAT WHEN YOU RETURN THEY BE NOT NEW TO YOU: THE KING WHO SENT HIS WIFE TO HER FATHER\'S HOUSE AND SAID, KEEP WEARING YOUR JEWELS; "SET UP MARKERS FOR YOURSELF" (JEREMIAH 31:20) — THE COMMANDMENTS BY WHICH ISRAEL IS MARKED; "SET UP SIGNPOSTS" — THE TEMPLE\'S DESTRUCTION, "IF I FORGET YOU, JERUSALEM" (PSALM 137:5-6); "SET YOUR HEART TO THE HIGHWAY" — SEE THE WAYS YOU WENT AND REPENT, AND AT ONCE YOU RETURN TO YOUR CITIES: "RETURN, VIRGIN ISRAEL". THE COMMANDMENTS ABROAD ({SP_(43, 34, "היו", "מצינים", "במצוות")} "be marked by the commandments"; {SP_(43, 34, "הציבי", "לך", "ציונים")} "set up markers for yourself"): E26 (checked) — the queen\'s jewels; 11:18\'s "put these My words" read as the exile\'s tefillin and mezuzot (44:1\'s rule the kin: the commandments of the body practised abroad); the sound-play markers / marked named. Fresh.')
srow(43, 35, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "AND YOU PERISH QUICKLY FROM OFF THE LAND" — FROM OFF THE GOOD LAND YOU ARE EXILED AND ENTER NO LAND AS GOOD. R. JUDAH: "GOOD" IS TORAH — "A GOOD DOCTRINE I GAVE YOU" (PROVERBS 4:2) IN THE LAND OF ISRAEL, "MY TORAH DO NOT FORSAKE" ABROAD. The piska\'s close ({SP_(43, 35, "טובה", "זו", "תורה")} "good — this is Torah"): the good land\'s "good" read as the Torah (the English marks a bracketed clause unattested — read and marked); Avot 6:3 in the note. Fresh.')

assert sorted(S) == [(43, r) for r in range(1, 36)], sorted(S)
